#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064246 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064100 :question/id #uuid "804f45cd-2082-5521-b4db-a32169716626" :question/math-academy-id "e-492" :question/problem "Calculate $\\displaystyle\\int x \\cos{2x}\\,\\textrm d x.$" :question/worked-solution "To solve this integral, we use the by-parts formula, given by\n\n$$\n\\int uv'\\,\\textrm{d}x= uv- \\int vu'\\,\\textrm{d}x.\n$$\n\nWe need to express $\\displaystyle \\int x \\cos{2x} \\textrm{d}x$ as $\\displaystyle \\int uv'\\,\\textrm{d}x.$ Therefore, we set\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=x\\, & ⟹\\,{u}^{′}=1 \\\\ {v}^{′}=\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x\\, & ⟹\\,v=\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe substitute the above into the integration by parts formula, and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x & =uv-\\int v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int x\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x\\,\\text{d}x & =x\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x-\\int \\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x\\cdot 1\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we calculate the integral, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int x\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{1}{2}x\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x-\\frac{1}{2}\\int \\operatorname{sin}⁡2x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}x\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x-\\frac{1}{2}(-\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x)+C \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}x\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x+\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x+C\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "bc6023d1-1461-50d1-b939-7e08f2878df4" :knowledge-point/key-prerequisites [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050489 :topic/math-academy-id 478 :topic/title "Integrating Trigonometric Functions Using Substitution"}] :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064484 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1af2e84f-a21d-52e3-a64a-4cd4f75a12e7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)}{9}+\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)}{3}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186257011} {:answer/id #uuid "9c127a15-e250-5fec-ba10-64265f125da9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)}{3}+\\frac{x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)}{9}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186258153} {:answer/id #uuid "a52d209e-bc78-5754-8593-120bb1521e79" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{(x+3)\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)}{3}+\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)}{9}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186258221} {:answer/id #uuid "ab28af47-d9d9-51e6-a7e7-784bf7544716" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{(x+3)\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)}{9}+\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)}{3}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186258275} {:answer/id #uuid "b11f0972-d6c7-5f7c-b041-100cfd94fdbd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{(x+3)\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)}{3}-\\frac{x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)}{3}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186258325}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a52d209e-bc78-5754-8593-120bb1521e79" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{(x+3)\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)}{3}+\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)}{9}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186258221} :answer-field/id #uuid "ec602d5e-cc1e-5573-8422-898b9eb55e75" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186259444}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "8f405e14-26e8-524b-b2bf-2f3fef1fc543" :question/math-academy-id "q-12564" :question/problem "$\\int (x+3)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)\\,\\text{d}x=$" :question/worked-solution "To solve this integral, we use the by-parts formula, given by\n\n$$\n\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x=uv-\\int v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nWe need to express $\\int (x+3)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)\\text{d}x$ as $\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x.$ Therefore, we set\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=x+3\\, & ⟹\\,{u}^{′}=1 \\\\ {v}^{′}=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)\\, & ⟹\\,v=\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe substitute the above into the integration by parts formula, and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x & =uv-\\int v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int (x+3)\\cdot \\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)\\,\\text{d}x & =(x+3)\\cdot \\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)}{3}-\\int \\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)}{3}\\cdot 1\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we calculate the integral, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int (x+3)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)\\text{d}x & =\\frac{(x+3)\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)}{3}-\\frac{1}{3}\\int \\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{(x+3)\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)}{3}+\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)}{9}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064509 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "043fa24a-45ec-5b10-bfa8-7e31faa50866" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2x\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186272422} {:answer/id #uuid "4dad317a-7e2c-5027-9a3a-188de187c660" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x-x\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186273038} {:answer/id #uuid "657c9906-4184-54b2-a2ca-75931266448c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x+x\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186273256} {:answer/id #uuid "cf6fa9bf-7209-5009-8683-0533f03518a8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x-\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186274192} {:answer/id #uuid "ef13a328-66f5-517d-8b0a-ca4c0258e019" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186274503}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ef13a328-66f5-517d-8b0a-ca4c0258e019" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186274503} :answer-field/id #uuid "8b869c77-052f-508f-90ff-9807f6d71398" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186274873}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "36f423a0-7a02-5e68-b537-f427610136e3" :question/math-academy-id "q-14437" :question/problem "Calculate $\\int 2x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)\\,\\text{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "To solve this integral, we use the by-parts formula, given by\n\n$$\n\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x=uv-\\int v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nWe need to express $\\int 2x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)\\text{d}x$ as $\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x.$ Therefore, we set\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=2x\\, & ⟹\\,{u}^{′}=2 \\\\ {v}^{′}=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)\\, & ⟹\\,v=-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe substitute the above into the integration by parts formula, and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x & =uv-\\int v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int 2x\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)\\,\\text{d}x & =2x\\cdot (-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x))-\\int (-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x))\\cdot 2\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we calculate the integral, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int 2x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)\\,\\text{d}x & =-2x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)+2\\int \\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-2x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)+2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)+C\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186250229 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6729e761-a109-51c4-8606-18751a53f95b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)+\\frac{x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)}{6}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248350} {:answer/id #uuid "8cf1abf3-9f83-5499-84e8-2cdbf9e21301" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)-\\frac{x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)}{3}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248682} {:answer/id #uuid "aeaf0778-2cce-5ff4-8bd6-a8910cbdb116" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)+\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)}{3}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248985} {:answer/id #uuid "bd3b4c5a-2810-58be-abbd-d2691adfd127" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)+\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)}{3}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249108} {:answer/id #uuid "c70e5714-4c05-5edb-b661-6e6122f8d589" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)}{3}-\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)}{9}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249190}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "bd3b4c5a-2810-58be-abbd-d2691adfd127" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)+\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)}{3}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249108} :answer-field/id #uuid "a7740ab9-c0ff-5f8c-91e3-87881adad76e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249964}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "a8a77892-fbcb-5fb9-802a-ce425028c881" :question/math-academy-id "q-114297" :question/problem "$\\int 3x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)\\,\\text{d}x=$" :question/worked-solution "To solve this integral, we use the by-parts formula, given by\n\n$$\n\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x=uv-\\int v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nWe need to express $\\int 3x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)\\text{d}x$ as $\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x.$ Therefore, we set\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=3x\\, & ⟹\\,{u}^{′}=3 \\\\ {v}^{′}=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)\\, & ⟹\\,v=\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe substitute the above into the integration by parts formula, and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x & =uv-\\int v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int 3x\\cdot \\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)\\,\\text{d}x & =3x\\cdot (\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)}{3})-\\int (\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)}{3})\\cdot 3\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we calculate the integral, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int 3x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)\\,\\text{d}x & =x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)-\\int \\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)+\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)}{3}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186250230 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "95bc501d-4124-5179-a51b-315ac85a1b36" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{x\\operatorname{sin}⁡4x}{2}+\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡4x}{8}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248757} {:answer/id #uuid "9f69fd84-e05c-5d24-ae8e-9d8f383459c1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3x\\operatorname{sin}⁡4x}{2}+\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡4x}{4}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248843} {:answer/id #uuid "dea80f9c-54f5-5396-b7ef-3e0d29ed1c4b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{x\\operatorname{sin}⁡4x}{4}-\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡4x}{2}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249399} {:answer/id #uuid "fc7731aa-f29b-5e06-aa8d-a528db3cff78" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡4x}{4}+\\frac{x\\operatorname{cos}⁡4x}{6}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249627} {:answer/id #uuid "ff931226-3ee2-5a37-af2b-7544f41260e5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡4x}{8}+\\frac{x\\operatorname{cos}⁡4x}{2}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249660}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "95bc501d-4124-5179-a51b-315ac85a1b36" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{x\\operatorname{sin}⁡4x}{2}+\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡4x}{8}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248757} :answer-field/id #uuid "75347d01-2014-547c-a5ad-13e10a343907" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249869}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "3b188b68-b90e-5d2a-a750-30bfecf83280" :question/math-academy-id "q-114299" :question/problem "Calculate $\\int 2x\\operatorname{cos}⁡4x\\,\\text{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "To solve this integral, we use the by-parts formula, given by\n\n$$\n\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x=uv-\\int v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nWe need to express $\\int 2x\\operatorname{cos}⁡4x\\text{d}x$ as $\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x.$ Therefore, we set\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=2x\\, & ⟹\\,{u}^{′}=2 \\\\ {v}^{′}=\\operatorname{cos}⁡4x\\, & ⟹\\,v=\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{sin}⁡4x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe substitute the above into the integration by parts formula, and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x & =uv-\\int v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int 2x\\operatorname{cos}⁡4x\\,\\text{d}x & =2x\\cdot \\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{sin}⁡4x-\\int \\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{sin}⁡4x\\cdot 2\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we calculate the integral, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int 2x\\operatorname{cos}⁡4x\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{1}{2}x\\operatorname{sin}⁡4x-\\frac{1}{2}\\int \\operatorname{sin}⁡4x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}x\\operatorname{sin}⁡4x-\\frac{1}{2}(-\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{cos}⁡4x)+C \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}x\\operatorname{sin}⁡4x+\\frac{1}{8}\\operatorname{cos}⁡4x+C\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186250233 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "21296bbd-9655-58f7-83aa-dba5af0c8f6e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{(x+4)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)}{2}+\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)}{4}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247716} {:answer/id #uuid "ab51dc5a-a926-51cd-8e7b-df0870f057c8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{3(x+4)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)}{2}+\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)}{6}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248946} {:answer/id #uuid "e5cbad19-d246-5b98-8980-41bddf12f22c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{(x+4)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)}{4}+\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)}{8}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249448} {:answer/id #uuid "e99bc9d8-a545-56d1-baef-23123e5ae336" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{(x+4)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)}{6}-\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)}{2}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249486} {:answer/id #uuid "f8073886-20e6-5ba4-879b-63835b53eb83" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{(x+4)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)}{4}-\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)}{2}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249586}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "21296bbd-9655-58f7-83aa-dba5af0c8f6e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{(x+4)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)}{2}+\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)}{4}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247716} :answer-field/id #uuid "6d9a9941-4c05-5900-9e9e-c028b2cee8de" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249858}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "64685827-c31f-5450-80d9-3d65e9e828de" :question/math-academy-id "q-114309" :question/problem "$\\int (x+4)\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)\\,\\text{d}x=$" :question/worked-solution "To solve this integral, we use the by-parts formula, given by\n\n$$\n\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x=uv-\\int v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nWe need to express $\\int (x+4)\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)\\text{d}x$ as $\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x.$ Therefore, we set\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=x+4\\, & ⟹\\,{u}^{′}=1 \\\\ {v}^{′}=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)\\, & ⟹\\,v=-\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe substitute the above into the integration by parts formula, and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x & =uv-\\int v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int (x+4)\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)\\,\\text{d}x & =(x+4)\\cdot (-\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)}{2})-\\int (-\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)}{2})\\cdot 1\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we calculate the integral, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int (x+4)\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)\\text{d}x & =-\\frac{(x+4)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)}{2}+\\frac{1}{2}\\int \\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-\\frac{(x+4)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)}{2}+\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)}{4}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186250234 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0847d4a6-8406-569f-8fd9-6ee28d2c43d6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-(2x+3)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)+2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247496} {:answer/id #uuid "9604a7f9-7867-5499-9942-d113f7cabdb5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)-6\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248760} {:answer/id #uuid "b4bb6439-052e-5829-9382-493c51eccdba" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(2x+3)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249041} {:answer/id #uuid "f40de5b1-3fd0-5afd-8a8c-b0a694969250" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)+4\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249561} {:answer/id #uuid "f9394f54-b364-5841-85eb-57a59630de67" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-(2x+3)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)-4\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249598}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0847d4a6-8406-569f-8fd9-6ee28d2c43d6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-(2x+3)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)+2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247496} :answer-field/id #uuid "5624c3ea-4def-51b8-a6da-e1cf8c816d71" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249828}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "a36b9441-9ddb-586c-961c-0956d2121b3c" :question/math-academy-id "q-114311" :question/problem "$\\int (2x+3)\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)\\,\\text{d}x=$" :question/worked-solution "To solve this integral, we use the by-parts formula, given by\n\n$$\n\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x=uv-\\int v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nWe need to express $\\int (2x+3)\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)\\text{d}x$ as $\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x.$ Therefore, we set\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=2x+3\\, & ⟹\\,{u}^{′}=2 \\\\ {v}^{′}=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)\\, & ⟹\\,v=-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe substitute the above into the integration by parts formula, and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x & =uv-\\int v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int (2x+3)\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)\\,\\text{d}x & =(2x+3)\\cdot (-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x))-\\int (-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x))\\cdot 2\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we calculate the integral, as follows\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int (2x+3)\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)\\text{d}x & =-(2x+3)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)+2\\int \\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-(2x+3)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)+2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)+C\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186250235 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7c09516b-ffde-5c4c-8dbe-564104924571" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5x)}{15}+\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5x)}{5}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248513} {:answer/id #uuid "a581301a-72c3-5cfb-8ef1-56abefe481a9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5x)}{25}+\\frac{x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5x)}{5}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248900} {:answer/id #uuid "a5873c57-b416-5bd2-86d9-681f98615c39" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5x)}{5}-\\frac{2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5x)}{25}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248901} {:answer/id #uuid "b120bf14-8c51-5072-89f4-30873910c7df" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5x)}{5}+\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5x)}{25}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249011} {:answer/id #uuid "d4ae0e29-77f1-5100-a586-609d2c797e98" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5x)}{5}-\\frac{x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5x)}{15}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249307}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b120bf14-8c51-5072-89f4-30873910c7df" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5x)}{5}+\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5x)}{25}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249011} :answer-field/id #uuid "3ea192b1-985a-504b-a59a-fe45ed09d88a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249781}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "6d0e94f6-1e93-555f-a728-ca5181d50236" :question/math-academy-id "q-114312" :question/problem "$\\int x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5x)\\,\\text{d}x=$" :question/worked-solution "To solve this integral, we use the by-parts formula, given by\n\n$$\n\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x=uv-\\int v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nWe need to express $\\int x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5x)\\text{d}x$ as $\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x.$ Therefore, we set\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=x\\, & ⟹\\,{u}^{′}=1 \\\\ {v}^{′}=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5x)\\, & ⟹\\,v=\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5x)}{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe substitute the above into the integration by parts formula, and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x & =uv-\\int v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int x\\cdot \\operatorname{cos}⁡(5x)\\,\\text{d}x & =x\\cdot (\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5x)}{5})-\\int (\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5x)}{5})\\cdot 1\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we calculate the integral, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5x)\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5x)}{5}-\\frac{1}{5}\\int \\operatorname{sin}⁡(5x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5x)}{5}+\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5x)}{25}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186250237 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1e07b070-117b-50c5-9563-364f2b472707" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\operatorname{tan}⁡x-\\operatorname{ln}⁡|\\operatorname{cos}⁡x|+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247691} {:answer/id #uuid "55dba241-a0ad-5dd2-a193-a8f4b6a32a61" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-x\\operatorname{cot}⁡x+\\operatorname{ln}⁡|\\operatorname{sin}⁡x|+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248201} {:answer/id #uuid "73e6af66-30b4-53c1-9d1f-0d00e757eaa3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-x\\operatorname{cot}⁡x-2\\operatorname{ln}⁡|\\operatorname{cos}⁡x|+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248442} {:answer/id #uuid "80fe39bd-6730-5d90-8ec2-9b32e504d4a5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\operatorname{tan}⁡x-2\\operatorname{ln}⁡|\\operatorname{sin}⁡x|+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248563} {:answer/id #uuid "fc349b75-7a3e-573b-affc-74cf566b5683" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2x\\operatorname{cot}⁡x-\\operatorname{ln}⁡|\\operatorname{sin}⁡x|+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249622}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "55dba241-a0ad-5dd2-a193-a8f4b6a32a61" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-x\\operatorname{cot}⁡x+\\operatorname{ln}⁡|\\operatorname{sin}⁡x|+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248201} :answer-field/id #uuid "c0fb41b9-ef63-543e-b53e-dffe53d28fbc" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186250000}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "ea7a186f-be1a-52b9-b47f-3320d955e3e8" :question/math-academy-id "q-114314" :question/problem "Calculate $\\int x{csc}^{2}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "To solve this integral, we use the by-parts formula, given by\n\n$$\n\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x=uv-\\int v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nWe need to express $\\int x{csc}^{2}⁡x\\text{d}x$ as $\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x.$ Therefore we set\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=x\\, & ⟹\\,{u}^{′}=1 \\\\ {v}^{′}={csc}^{2}⁡x\\, & ⟹\\,v=-\\operatorname{cot}⁡x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe substitute the above into the integration by parts formula, and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x & =uv-\\int v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int x\\cdot {csc}^{2}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x & =x\\cdot (-\\operatorname{cot}⁡x)-\\int (-\\operatorname{cot}⁡x)\\cdot 1\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-x\\operatorname{cot}⁡x+\\int \\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we calculate the integral using the substitution $u=\\operatorname{sin}⁡x,$ where $\\text{d}u=\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int x{csc}^{2}⁡(x)\\,\\text{d}x & =-x\\operatorname{cot}⁡x+\\int \\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-x\\operatorname{cot}⁡x+\\int \\frac{1}{u}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =-x\\operatorname{cot}⁡x+\\operatorname{ln}⁡|u|+C \\\\  & =-x\\operatorname{cot}⁡x+\\operatorname{ln}⁡|\\operatorname{sin}⁡x|+C\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186275151 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0532f827-efa9-5943-921e-cd8747195164" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{cos}⁡5x+x\\operatorname{sin}⁡5x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186272435} {:answer/id #uuid "a34610b7-078b-5a23-bfdf-b83fba68fb35" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-5x\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186273796} {:answer/id #uuid "aa05f3bb-4c79-5366-99b2-4194d18ca74e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x-\\operatorname{cos}⁡5x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186273855} {:answer/id #uuid "ad550bfa-33c2-5773-873f-42e48064e922" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-5x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+5\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186273882} {:answer/id #uuid "c15bdd0d-cf56-529b-ba9a-ea8d3c6be943" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x-x\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186274066}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ad550bfa-33c2-5773-873f-42e48064e922" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-5x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+5\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186273882} :answer-field/id #uuid "4eeb4dbf-b5b3-5475-acd4-8a11aa7e8123" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186274768}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "633e79f5-4963-57db-9237-badf9fbf96a9" :question/math-academy-id "q-14449" :question/problem "Calculate $\\int 5x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)\\,\\text{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "To solve this integral, we use the by-parts formula, given by\n\n$$\n\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x=uv-\\int v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nWe need to express $\\int 5x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)\\text{d}x$ as $\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x.$ Therefore, we set\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=5x\\, & ⟹\\,{u}^{′}=5 \\\\ {v}^{′}=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)\\, & ⟹\\,v=-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe substitute the above into the integration by parts formula, and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x & =uv-\\int v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int 5x\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)\\,\\text{d}x & =5x\\cdot (-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x))-\\int (-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x))\\cdot 5\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we calculate the integral, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int 5x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)\\,\\text{d}x & =-5x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)+5\\int \\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-5x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)+5\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)+C\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186275152 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "06faa5e0-4af8-5348-9efd-11165c5b749d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-6x\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+6\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186272448} {:answer/id #uuid "316a580c-b1ad-519a-9924-7acafc208775" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\operatorname{cos}⁡6x+x\\operatorname{sin}⁡6x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186272829} {:answer/id #uuid "515140df-a38b-5675-b2b8-0083349b8513" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\operatorname{cos}⁡6x-x\\operatorname{sin}⁡6x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186273080} {:answer/id #uuid "632167df-25c2-51dc-8e43-73f4595dd519" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-6x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186273239} {:answer/id #uuid "e8961a49-7238-5263-89a6-7dc02e214375" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6x\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+6\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186274443}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e8961a49-7238-5263-89a6-7dc02e214375" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6x\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+6\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186274443} :answer-field/id #uuid "00d03065-2e89-51a1-b42e-23e110a6964b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186274638}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "efa8bb83-66d2-57ab-8d51-71c6b76f0e3c" :question/math-academy-id "q-14453" :question/problem "$\\int 6x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)\\,\\text{d}x=$" :question/worked-solution "To solve this integral, we use the by-parts formula, given by\n\n$$\n\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x=uv-\\int v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nWe need to express $\\int 6x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)\\text{d}x$ as $\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x.$ Therefore, we set\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=6x\\, & ⟹\\,{u}^{′}=6 \\\\ {v}^{′}=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)\\, & ⟹\\,v=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe substitute the above into the integration by parts formula, and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x & =uv-\\int v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int 6x\\cdot \\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)\\,\\text{d}x & =6x\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)-\\int \\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)\\cdot 6\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we calculate the integral, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int 6x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)\\,\\text{d}x & =6x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)-6\\int \\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =6x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)-6(-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x))+C \\\\  & =6x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)+6\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)+C\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186342146 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "13c9bf20-8128-53fc-aa86-1964b815386d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x+8)+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x+8)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339304} {:answer/id #uuid "4eeb7e5b-2acb-5ebe-ad55-584b08e3b9c7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x+8)+\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x+8)}{2}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339845} {:answer/id #uuid "534af3da-95e9-55b2-aba8-6f4b454b8ad9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x+8)-\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x+8)}{4}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339896} {:answer/id #uuid "90dc551e-639b-50fc-9023-134528ddbdd4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x+8)+\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x+8)}{2}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340425} {:answer/id #uuid "c5917a7f-b9e8-5505-bca8-86a9c397ec2c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x+8)-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x+8)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340880}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4eeb7e5b-2acb-5ebe-ad55-584b08e3b9c7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x+8)+\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x+8)}{2}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339845} :answer-field/id #uuid "64dee0d1-0120-5112-8fc9-ab060cbba4c9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186341556}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "6203036f-b82a-557b-b713-2351ced43cc7" :question/math-academy-id "q-74087" :question/problem "Calculate  $\\int 2x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x+8)\\text{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "To solve this integral, we use the by-parts formula, given by\n\n$$\n\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x=uv-\\int v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nWe need to express $\\int 2x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x+8)\\text{d}x$ as $\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x.$ Therefore, we set\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=2x\\, & ⟹\\,{u}^{′}=2 \\\\ {v}^{′}=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x+8)\\, & ⟹\\,v=\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x+8)}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe substitute the above into the integration by parts formula, and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x & =uv-\\int v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int 2x\\cdot \\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x+8)\\,\\text{d}x & =2x\\cdot \\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x+8)}{2}-\\int \\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x+8)}{2}\\cdot 2\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we calculate the integral, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int 2x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x+8)\\text{d}x & =x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x+8)-\\int \\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x+8)\\text{d}x \\\\  & =x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x+8)+\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x+8)}{2}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186342147 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1d4e53ff-430e-5b10-b738-cd8dd3d0256b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339385} {:answer/id #uuid "4b9151d3-7fde-540f-b82e-0580c7384593" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(6x+1)\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)+\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)}{6}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339807} {:answer/id #uuid "989f6c04-735e-50e5-8fdd-bb014b8275b8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)+6\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340506} {:answer/id #uuid "add28c3c-0b54-53af-97fb-51c4b2116412" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(6x+1)\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)+6\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340712} {:answer/id #uuid "f90418c6-311c-5a49-b4cf-0366851ed196" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{(6x+1)\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)}{6}+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186341332}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "add28c3c-0b54-53af-97fb-51c4b2116412" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(6x+1)\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)+6\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340712} :answer-field/id #uuid "0614f8dc-7023-5386-a910-5a8612abf41b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186341396}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "b94b38f3-a670-562e-93ec-c45c6d3b0d77" :question/math-academy-id "q-74088" :question/problem "$\\int (6x+1)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)\\,\\text{d}x=$" :question/worked-solution "To solve this integral, we use the by-parts formula, given by\n\n$$\n\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x=uv-\\int v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nWe need to express $\\int (6x+1)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)\\text{d}x$ as $\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x.$ Therefore, we set\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=6x+1\\, & ⟹\\,{u}^{′}=6 \\\\ {v}^{′}=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)\\, & ⟹\\,v=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe substitute the above into the integration by parts formula, and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x & =uv-\\int v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int (6x+1)\\cdot \\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)\\,\\text{d}x & =(6x+1)\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)-\\int \\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)\\cdot 6\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we calculate the integral, as follows\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int (6x+1)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)\\text{d}x & =(6x+1)\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)-6\\int \\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =(6x+1)\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)+6\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)+C\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186342148 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0e99b757-9d06-5cfc-8db6-a2492878332c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)}{10}-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339262} {:answer/id #uuid "3a4fd180-d811-5662-8d7f-8cf39e6abded" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)+\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)}{10}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339651} {:answer/id #uuid "73d61482-1a92-5fde-a598-f549899e13ee" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)+10\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340154} {:answer/id #uuid "b2f2d102-e8a3-564e-981d-58e57522a465" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)-10x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340754} {:answer/id #uuid "da9ff3c8-cb06-5827-af7c-d34ff6bef005" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186341070}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "73d61482-1a92-5fde-a598-f549899e13ee" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)+10\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340154} :answer-field/id #uuid "e6a2565c-7c88-5b3a-b2f9-3d057c775bea" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186341789}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "31ac68e1-bc05-5634-b712-63c327f4e3c2" :question/math-academy-id "q-74090" :question/problem "Calculate $\\int 10x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)\\,\\text{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "To solve this integral, we use the by-parts formula, given by\n\n$$\n\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x=uv-\\int v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nWe need to express $\\int 10x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)\\text{d}x$ as $\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x.$ Therefore, we set\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=10x\\, & ⟹\\,{u}^{′}=10 \\\\ {v}^{′}=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)\\, & ⟹\\,v=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe substitute the above into the integration by parts formula, and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x & =uv-\\int v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int 10x\\cdot \\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)\\,\\text{d}x & =10x\\cdot (\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x))-\\int (\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x))\\cdot 10\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we calculate the integral, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int 10x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)\\,\\text{d}x & =10x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)-10\\int \\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =10x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)+10\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)+C\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186363003 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9775c1a1-be1f-5d4a-8b38-2b22b3877645" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{3x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x+5)}{3}+\\frac{3\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x+5)}{9}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363005} {:answer/id #uuid "25af2b05-29e6-557b-85e3-77fd7abe9e44" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x+5)}{3}+\\frac{x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x+5)}{9}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363006} {:answer/id #uuid "91cb4a25-ae24-57be-8930-89439bfcd808" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x+5)}{3}+\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x+5)}{9}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363007} {:answer/id #uuid "e1b7d50e-bf4c-5d3c-8f65-093e0d804de6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x+5)}{9}-\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x+5)}{3}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363008} {:answer/id #uuid "b9c244ca-ce7e-5f14-8b4e-fc2f90fec15c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x+5)}{9}+\\frac{2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x+5)}{9}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363009}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "91cb4a25-ae24-57be-8930-89439bfcd808" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x+5)}{3}+\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x+5)}{9}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363007} :answer-field/id #uuid "9d5a6fdb-0204-5d6b-854a-5929492322cb" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363004}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "6d889fae-ff07-5704-acc9-b1fed02f79be" :question/math-academy-id "q-12565" :question/problem "Calculate  $\\int x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x+5)\\text{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "To solve this integral, we use the by-parts formula, given by\n\n$$\n\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x=uv-\\int v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nWe need to express $\\int x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x+5)\\text{d}x$ as $\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x.$ Therefore, we set\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=x\\, & ⟹\\,{u}^{′}=1 \\\\ {v}^{′}=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x+5)\\, & ⟹\\,v=-\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x+5)}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe, substitute the above into the integration by parts formula, and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x & =uv-\\int v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int x\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x+5)\\,\\text{d}x & =x\\cdot (-\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x+5)}{3})-\\int (-\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x+5)}{3})\\cdot 1\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we calculate the integral, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x+5)\\text{d}x & =-\\frac{x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x+5)}{3}+\\frac{1}{3}\\int \\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x+5)\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-\\frac{x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x+5)}{3}+\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x+5)}{9}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186367603 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b416a21d-f860-5ddd-9887-3909cbcfc268" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)}{4}-\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)}{4}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186367605} {:answer/id #uuid "84ff0b6d-4bc8-58b4-8c1f-7733a5d10ac0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)+\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)}{2}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186367606} {:answer/id #uuid "8e61b06f-5796-5daf-a560-740f317dd6f5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4x)}{4}+\\frac{x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4x)}{4}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186367607} {:answer/id #uuid "52c4db08-6d75-5662-ba65-98e14935cb32" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)}{2}+\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)}{4}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186367608} {:answer/id #uuid "665ef108-98da-5b42-b5b6-51f12caa5073" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)}{4}+\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)}{2}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186367609}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "84ff0b6d-4bc8-58b4-8c1f-7733a5d10ac0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)+\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)}{2}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186367606} :answer-field/id #uuid "7906d722-793f-554d-8af3-30e86eebaf11" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186367604}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "c948087e-b394-5663-8b66-c2d6a56d25e1" :question/math-academy-id "q-14451" :question/problem "$\\int 2x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)\\,\\text{d}x=$" :question/worked-solution "To solve this integral, we use the by-parts formula, given by\n\n$$\n\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x=uv-\\int v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nWe need to express $\\int 2x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)\\text{d}x$ as $\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x.$ Therefore, we set\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=2x\\, & ⟹\\,{u}^{′}=2 \\\\ {v}^{′}=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)\\, & ⟹\\,v=-\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe substitute the above into the integration by parts formula, and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x & =uv-\\int v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int 2x\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)\\,\\text{d}x & =2x\\cdot (-\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)}{2})-\\int (-\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)}{2})\\cdot 2\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we calculate the integral, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int 2x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)\\,\\text{d}x & =-x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)+\\int \\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)+\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)}{2}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] :knowledge-point/title "Using Integration by Parts to Compute an Indefinite Integral Containing a Trigonometric Expression"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064271 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064114 :question/id #uuid "5831f44c-02c6-5a5b-a9e7-58c7ac36cb6d" :question/math-academy-id "e-6112" :question/problem "A rocket is at a distance of $r(t)$ meters from the ground $t$ seconds after it is launched. What are the units of $\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}r}{\\textrm{d}t}?$" :question/worked-solution "We have that the height $r(t)$ is measured in meters and the time is measured in seconds. \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r(t): & \\text{meters} \\\\ t: & \\text{seconds}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe derivative $\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}r}{\\textrm{d}t}$ measures a change in $r(t)$ over a change in $t.$ So, it represents a ratio of the units:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}t}: & \\frac{\\text{meters}}{\\text{seconds}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}r}{\\textrm{d}t}$ is measured in \"meters per second\"."} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "0fa5bdf9-4b27-5565-9ee1-ecb9f9db4791" :knowledge-point/key-prerequisites [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049092 :topic/math-academy-id 2231 :topic/title "Selecting Units for Rates of Change"}] :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064826 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "84db6e6b-7217-5d54-9e58-abd0eb0b10b7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "dollar per ton squared" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186063014} {:answer/id #uuid "a75c3b50-fff3-5adf-8644-677a0a92aacc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "dollar per ton" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186063015} {:answer/id #uuid "c7b8d11d-9c03-5c05-af46-dbd29075cb5a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "tons" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186063016} {:answer/id #uuid "f8200aa2-2409-5b8d-9519-f8c9e8da9833" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "dollars" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186063017} {:answer/id #uuid "0dcadfb8-535c-5641-a89b-aa53b62d5c6c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "tons per dollar" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186063018}] :answer-field/id #uuid "f0d0b77e-7751-5d6c-827e-92e46aef931f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186063013}] :question/id #uuid "3e0ede41-0db9-5bed-9ceb-b602ec6e0c54" :question/math-academy-id "q-48557" :question/problem "A farmer estimates that she can sell $w(p)$ metric tons of crops at a price of $p$ dollars per ton. What are the units of $\\frac{dw}{dp}$?"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064829 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "92421c81-ee97-5a10-bf38-61a0e0bc8008" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "seconds" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186063032} {:answer/id #uuid "9a0d7c98-d4a4-5498-a083-52a1c935dfe0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "centimeters per second" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186063033} {:answer/id #uuid "32cb3a36-7b13-584a-aac4-956bfd56985e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "centimeters" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186063034} {:answer/id #uuid "653a2b6c-4c78-5ce2-8d08-0320e0e42144" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "cubic centimeters per second" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186063035} {:answer/id #uuid "6fab13b0-d7b9-5e22-bdfb-c394c79be9ed" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "seconds per cubic centimeter" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186063036}] :answer-field/id #uuid "437de520-ea14-5a91-9db3-48216a3ed68a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186063031}] :question/id #uuid "65e27d8d-ce3f-5fb9-a70c-1dd4d9ab0259" :question/math-academy-id "q-48613" :question/problem "The volume of water in a pail $t$ seconds after it starts filling with water is $V(t)$ cubic centimeters. What are the units of $\\frac{dV}{dt}$?"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186233124 :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "8bf27617-88ec-528e-ace5-0ea42a142d27" :question/math-academy-id "q-110040" :question/problem "A website receives $v(h)$ visits every $h$ hours. What are the units of $\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}h}?$" :question/worked-solution "We have that the time $h$ is measured in hours and the number of visits is measured in visitors. \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}h: & \\text{hours} \\\\ v(h): & \\text{visitors}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe derivative $\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}h}$ measures a change in $v$ over a change in $h.$ So, it represents a ratio of the units:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}h}: & \\frac{\\text{visitors}}{\\text{hours}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn other words, $\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}h}$ is measured in \"visitors per hour \"."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186234316 :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "e20bdb49-6bfd-500e-8f84-fa81ea81c70a" :question/math-academy-id "q-72091" :question/problem "A student's parents promise to reward her $R(p)$ dollars if she obtains an average of $p$ points in her exams. What are the units of $\\frac{\\text{d}R}{\\text{d}p}?$" :question/worked-solution "We have that the student's reward $R(p)$ is measured in dollars and the average exam result is measured in points. \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}R(p): & \\text{dollars} \\\\ p: & \\text{points}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe derivative $\\frac{\\text{d}R}{\\text{d}p}$ measures a change in $R(p)$ over a change in $p.$ So, it represents a ratio of the units:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}R}{\\text{d}p}: & \\frac{\\text{dollars}}{\\text{points}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn other words, $\\frac{\\text{d}R}{\\text{d}p}$ is measured in \"dollars per point\"."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186247072 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1432e650-2a84-5de8-9f60-1d496025ae15" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "squared kilograms per cupcake" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186244499} {:answer/id #uuid "230632ba-b376-58f5-b0ba-12899458008e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "cupcakes per kilogram" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186244622} {:answer/id #uuid "9d0e3fc8-6ea7-54d4-b5a5-cd0ff85c5eb4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "kilograms per cupcake" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245710} {:answer/id #uuid "9d75aea8-62f4-5f4d-aeb3-1c234eacd0b0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "grams per cupcake" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245715} {:answer/id #uuid "bb7ffb51-25e8-521e-8889-98bb404c734a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "cupcakes per gram" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245986}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9d75aea8-62f4-5f4d-aeb3-1c234eacd0b0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "grams per cupcake" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245715} :answer-field/id #uuid "3647db23-f4d0-5781-a4e9-437c732d9642" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186246639}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "77542117-c7f0-50c4-8cf0-8d65753dc3a2" :question/math-academy-id "q-110037" :question/problem "Mary bakes $c$ cupcakes using $f(c)$ grams of flour. What are the units of $\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}c}?$" :question/worked-solution "We have that the amount of flour $f(c)$ is measured in grams and the number of cupcakes is measured in cupcakes. \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(c): & \\text{grams} \\\\ c: & \\text{cupcakes}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe derivative $\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}c}$ measures a change in $f(c)$ over a change in $c.$ So, it represents a ratio of the units:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}c}: & \\frac{\\text{grams}}{\\text{cupcake}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}c}$ is measured in \"grams per cupcake\"."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186247073 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2cb3deab-5eae-5535-968a-2d1e22dcf28d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "milliliters per squared dollar" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186244714} {:answer/id #uuid "61b09bf2-e29b-53ee-b371-9f83642f4791" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "dollars per liter" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245169} {:answer/id #uuid "a3d8ef65-5e83-5666-a91c-daf321781d87" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "liters per dollar" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245777} {:answer/id #uuid "de708a99-58c4-54ca-b39c-3a9b08df0767" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "dollars per milliliter" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186246285} {:answer/id #uuid "f9ca274e-81bc-562e-ac57-2c8de33f82dd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "cubic dollars per squared liters" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186246507}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "61b09bf2-e29b-53ee-b371-9f83642f4791" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "dollars per liter" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245169} :answer-field/id #uuid "e8f7ae07-db8a-5e42-bdd2-e92de378204b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186246960}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "cc012d6e-17d6-5b41-813e-869311eeed2b" :question/math-academy-id "q-110038" :question/problem "A dairy farm sells milk on a particular day for $p(v)$ dollars, where $v$ is the number of liters of milk in the dairy farm at the start of the day. What are the units of $\\frac{\\text{d}p}{\\text{d}v}?$" :question/worked-solution "We have that the price $p(v)$ is measured in dollars and the volume of milk is measured in liters. \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p(v): & \\text{dollars} \\\\ v: & \\text{liters}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe derivative $\\frac{\\text{d}p}{\\text{d}v}$ measures a change in $p(v)$ over a change in $v.$ So, it represents a ratio of the units:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}p}{\\text{d}v}: & \\frac{\\text{dollars}}{\\text{liters}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn other words, $\\frac{\\text{d}p}{\\text{d}v}$ is measured in \"dollars per liter\"."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186247074 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0a9d1daa-4262-5139-a82a-fa3e67db2278" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "squared hours" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186244405} {:answer/id #uuid "14b30c62-666a-59b5-8d86-70c3aaa84281" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "hours per minute" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186244504} {:answer/id #uuid "266712ff-2378-5f67-aec9-f0527b04aad3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "minutes" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186244654} {:answer/id #uuid "b676b7d4-a1ba-50cd-8d9e-e05b06adc11f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "hours" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245944} {:answer/id #uuid "f0f28c2d-9b38-50b8-86c4-fef300c2b50e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "minutes per hour" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186246441}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "14b30c62-666a-59b5-8d86-70c3aaa84281" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "hours per minute" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186244504} :answer-field/id #uuid "05a9c882-cc73-506a-8893-344eaeecc41b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186246562}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "986c7828-ebef-5b92-b3ca-04f414e27f95" :question/math-academy-id "q-110042" :question/problem "A battery lasts $L(t)$ hours when it is charged for $t$ minutes. What are the units of $\\frac{\\text{d}L}{\\text{d}t}?$" :question/worked-solution "We have that the battery duration $L(t)$ is measured in hours and the charging time is measured in minutes. \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L(t): & \\text{hours} \\\\ t: & \\text{minutes}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe derivative $\\frac{\\text{d}L}{\\text{d}t}$ measures a change in $L(t)$ over a change in $t.$ So, it represents a ratio of the units:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}L}{\\text{d}t}: & \\frac{\\text{hours}}{\\text{minute}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn other words, $\\frac{\\text{d}L}{\\text{d}t}$ is measured in \"hours per minute\"."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186339057 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "191efa1b-34c1-5365-be3b-25ddf4b0878a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "dollars" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186336266} {:answer/id #uuid "7a27ba9e-1595-5cb8-a697-d76669bb1794" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "euros per dollar" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337132} {:answer/id #uuid "b91d68db-20eb-5f96-9c8a-9f6af0eab16a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "dollars per euro squared" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337673} {:answer/id #uuid "d86a958e-469e-511d-86db-bafff552c3b9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "dollars per euro" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337911} {:answer/id #uuid "e341cd72-3449-5c1e-a7b1-d6dc23dcd304" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "euros" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338014}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7a27ba9e-1595-5cb8-a697-d76669bb1794" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "euros per dollar" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337132} :answer-field/id #uuid "2888a3c8-cb45-5467-a5e7-8b319bd9aa94" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338354}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "13af356c-d230-584b-ad7a-58e4b56fa385" :question/math-academy-id "q-72092" :question/problem "A bank exchanges $D$ dollars for $E(D)$ euros. What are the units of $\\frac{\\text{d}E}{\\text{d}D}?$" :question/worked-solution "We have that the currency $E(D)$ is measured in euros and the currency $D$ is measured in dollars. \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}E(D): & \\text{euros} \\\\ D: & \\text{dollars}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe derivative $\\frac{\\text{d}E}{\\text{d}D}$ measures a change in $E(D)$ over a change in $D.$ So, it represents a ratio of the units:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}E}{\\text{d}D}: & \\frac{\\text{euros}}{\\text{dollars}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn other words, $\\frac{\\text{d}E}{\\text{d}D}$ is measured in \"euros per dollar\"."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186402984 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "edec9b0f-e74f-5f71-8e01-c49ef9dcd993" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "Degrees Fahrenheit per minute" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186402986} {:answer/id #uuid "f6d4c614-ec2d-5d40-969c-a53c3dd207e0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "Degrees Fahrenheit" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186402987} {:answer/id #uuid "4ec8af8b-c1c2-588d-b21b-584e7bda5fb3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "Minutes per degrees Fahrenheit" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186402988} {:answer/id #uuid "c8dada28-2d89-5b17-8652-6cc73bf5852f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "Minutes" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186402989} {:answer/id #uuid "9dc2b148-ac18-514b-b0ae-11c7d6164436" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "Degrees Fahrenheit squared per minute" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186402990}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "edec9b0f-e74f-5f71-8e01-c49ef9dcd993" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "Degrees Fahrenheit per minute" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186402986} :answer-field/id #uuid "ad3df16f-9c93-57df-88a3-0c0fe3164587" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186402985}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "453a4f9f-dc2c-5ef4-9ab6-f86f7acd693b" :question/math-academy-id "q-48611" :question/problem "A cup of coffee sitting on a teacher's desk $t$ minutes after it has been made has the temperature $F(t)$ degrees Fahrenheit. What are the units of $\\frac{\\text{d}F}{\\text{d}t}?$" :question/worked-solution "We have that the temperature $F(t)$ is measured in degrees Fahrenheit and the time is measured in minutes. \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(t): & \\text{degrees Fahrenheit} \\\\ t: & \\text{minutes}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe derivative $\\frac{\\text{d}F}{\\text{d}t}$ measures a change in $F(t)$ over a change in $t.$ So, it represents a ratio of the units:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}F}{\\text{d}t}: & \\frac{\\text{degrees Fahrenheit}}{\\text{minutes}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $\\frac{\\text{d}F}{\\text{d}t}$ is measured in \"degrees Fahrenheit per minute\"."}] :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Units of a Derivative"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064272 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064115 :question/id #uuid "0f4baedc-a28a-5b45-97d7-d7e1196b21c2" :question/math-academy-id "e-6113" :question/problem "Howard, the manager of a sci-fi convention, uses the following three functions to model the daily number of visitors to the convention, $t$ minutes after the convention has opened.\n\n- $N(t)$ - the number of people inside the convention\n\n- $E(t)$ - the rate at which people enter the convention\n\n- $L(t)$ - the rate at which people leave the convention\n\nWhat is the relationship between the three functions above?" :question/worked-solution "The function $N(t)$ gives the number of people inside the convention $t$ minutes after opening. Then,\n\n$$\nN'(t) = \\dfrac{\\textrm{d}N(t)}{\\textrm{d}t} = \\dfrac{\\textrm{Change in }N}{\\textrm{Change in }t}.\n$$\n\nThus, $N'(t)$ gives the rate at which the number of people inside the convention changes $t$ minutes after opening.\n\nIn addition, we can compute the rate of change of the number of people inside the convention at time $t$ by finding the difference between the entry and exit rates at time $t.$ That is,\n\n$$\nN'(t) = E(t) - L(t).\n$$"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "fa38f112-466c-50e9-ac08-be72b6f53782" :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064837 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "91bce12a-a0ee-508e-9b44-1a9e82a75aac" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "N(t) = E(t) + L(t)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186063080} {:answer/id #uuid "b02d1fbd-19a0-587f-9cb3-faede4da052a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "N^{′}(t) = E(t) - L(t)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186063081} {:answer/id #uuid "e83c99ce-81ce-59b5-aa52-e240f898c1f7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "N^{′}(t) = E(t) \\cdot L(t)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186063082} {:answer/id #uuid "ef02aea9-a9c5-59f2-b08a-0b8813557b4c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "N^{′}(t) = E(t) + L(t)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186063083} {:answer/id #uuid "0fe4eed2-52a7-5fd3-a1c6-cdae319434fc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "N(t) = E(t) - L(t)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186063084}] :answer-field/id #uuid "9ec4ed13-bf56-57c0-afef-d9dca073a67b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186063079}] :question/id #uuid "a8bc5d1f-a3ab-5829-b912-fad0a50e9612" :question/math-academy-id "q-48707" :question/problem "Susan, the new receptionist of the Smithsonian Museum in Washington DC, uses the following three functions to model the daily number of visitors to the museum $t$ minutes after the museum has opened.\n\n- $N(t)$ - the number of people inside the museum\n- $E(t)$ - the rate at which people enter the museum\n- $L(t)$ - the rate at which people leave the museum\n\nWhat is the relationship between the three functions above?"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064947 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "148eb00f-3a9c-5cde-b11e-4aa6e5df5baf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "N(t)=r(t)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186336227} {:answer/id #uuid "3ce9ccdf-1421-5fcb-b41e-795e91107452" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "N(t)={r}^{′}(t)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186336606} {:answer/id #uuid "3d4ac506-d0f2-599b-b8f3-e6dce6983161" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{N}^{′}(t)=r(t)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186336611} {:answer/id #uuid "80a522d2-bd93-5515-9735-bcaf1eb17692" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "N(t)=-{r}^{′}(t)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337197} {:answer/id #uuid "e3743113-4ad5-561d-af41-cbb9230afbba" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{N}^{′}(t)=-r(t)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338017}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3d4ac506-d0f2-599b-b8f3-e6dce6983161" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{N}^{′}(t)=r(t)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186336611} :answer-field/id #uuid "874c5434-9157-538e-be59-176244d35d61" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338525}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "97f8f938-0d50-59f5-922b-f7bea8bb44f7" :question/math-academy-id "q-72004" :question/problem "Jason, a biologist, is measuring the growth of bacteria in a Petri dish by recording the following two numbers for different values of $t,$ where $t$ is the time, in hours, since he started his observations:\n\n- $N(t)$ - the number of bacteria in the dish.\n\n- $r(t)$ - the rate at which the number of bacteria in the dish is increasing.\n\nWhat is the relationship between $N(t)$ and $r(t)?$" :question/worked-solution "The function $N(t)$ gives the number of bacteria inside the dish after $t$ hours. Then,\n\n$$\n{N}^{′}(t)=\\frac{\\text{d}N(t)}{\\text{d}t}=\\frac{\\text{Change in }N}{\\text{Change in }t}.\n$$\n\nThus, ${N}^{′}(t)$ gives the rate at which the number of bacteria is increasing at time $t$, which is the same as $r(t).$ Therefore, the relationship between $N(t)$ and $r(t)$ is ${N}^{′}(t)=r(t).$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186233149 :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "539cfdfe-838f-5f01-80a7-fcde0e816b91" :question/math-academy-id "q-112509" :question/problem "Joseph is measuring the height reached by his lime tree by recording the following two numbers for different values of $t,$ where $t$ is the time, in years, since he planted the tree:\n\n- $H(t)$ - The tree's height, in centimeters\n\n- $r(t)$ - the rate at which the tree's height is increasing.\n\nWhat is the relationship between $H(t)$ and $r(t)?$" :question/worked-solution "The function $H(t)$ gives the tree's height after $t$ years. Then,\n\n$$\n{H}^{'}(t)=\\frac{\\text{d}H(t)}{\\text{d}t}=\\frac{\\text{Change in }H}{\\text{Change in }t}.\n$$\n\nThus, ${H}^{'}(t)$ gives the rate at which the height of the tree increases at time $t$, which is the same as $r(t).$ Therefore, the relationship between $H(t)$ and $r(t)$ is ${H}^{'}(t)=r(t).$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186234105 :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "c00a28ec-ae50-52ff-8f5b-35e535d7e4c4" :question/math-academy-id "q-48923" :question/problem "To measure the success of an amusement park, Ed uses the following three functions that model the daily number of visitors to the park $t$ minutes after the park is opened to the public.\n\n- $N(t)$ - the number of people inside the park\n\n- $E(t)$ - the rate at which people enter the park\n\n- $L(t)$ - the rate at which people leave the park\n\nWhat is the relationship between the functions above?" :question/worked-solution "The function $N(t)$ gives the number of people inside the park $t$ minutes after opening. Then,\n\n$$\n{N}^{'}(t)=\\frac{\\text{d}N(t)}{\\text{d}t}=\\frac{\\text{Change in }N}{\\text{Change in }t}.\n$$\n\nThus, ${N}^{'}(t)$ gives the rate at which the number of people inside the park changes $t$ minutes after opening.\n\nIn addition, we can compute the rate of change of the number of people inside the park at time $t$ by finding the difference between the entry and exit rates at time $t.$ That is,\n\n$$\n{N}^{'}(t)=E(t)-L(t).\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186234317 :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "11f79d9f-7e6c-5c8e-9aff-c762fbcfd4b7" :question/math-academy-id "q-72109" :question/problem "Ramin, a bricklayer, is monitoring the construction of a wall by recording the following two numbers for different values of $t,$ where $t$ is the time, in hours, since he started his observations:\n\n- $B(t)$ - the number of bricks in the wall.\n\n- $r(t)$ - the rate at which the number of bricks in the wall is increasing.\n\nWhat is the relationship between $B(t)$ and $r(t)?$" :question/worked-solution "The function $B(t)$ gives the number of bricks inside the wall after $t$ hours. Then,\n\n$$\n{B}^{'}(t)=\\frac{\\text{d}B(t)}{\\text{d}t}=\\frac{\\text{Change in }B}{\\text{Change in }t}.\n$$\n\nThus, ${B}^{'}(t)$ gives the rate at which the number of bricks increases at time $t$, which is the same as $r(t).$ Therefore, the relationship between $B(t)$ and $r(t)$ is ${B}^{'}(t)=r(t).$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186247283 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "10ee469f-3408-5fe2-92e1-b73437f736b4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{P}^{′}(t)=\\frac{1}{r(t)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186244471} {:answer/id #uuid "3c6ca379-be1f-59bb-b575-764bd123d07e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "P(t)={r}^{2}(t)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186244845} {:answer/id #uuid "3fcf123c-f946-58b3-95ea-c7435a4f1def" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{P}^{′}(t)=r(t)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186244873} {:answer/id #uuid "6d60a78d-cfd5-5840-9657-df2315347309" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "P(t)={r}^{′}(t)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245280} {:answer/id #uuid "e067d9ea-1418-5133-aff0-81b214ce0135" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{P}^{′}(t)=1-r(t)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186246308}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3fcf123c-f946-58b3-95ea-c7435a4f1def" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{P}^{′}(t)=r(t)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186244873} :answer-field/id #uuid "2bc9aea5-67df-59f8-abb7-e8249f8d9def" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186246618}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "59ff5d13-6b87-5fe2-a8ce-d480b49dc41c" :question/math-academy-id "q-112518" :question/problem "Liam, a farmer, is monitoring the construction of a fence by recording the following two numbers for different values of $t,$ where $t$ is the time, in hours, since he started his observations:\n\n- $P(t)$ - the number of panels in the fence.\n\n- $r(t)$ - the rate at which the number of panels in the fence increases.\n\nWhat is the relationship between $P(t)$ and $r(t)?$" :question/worked-solution "The function $P(t)$ gives the number of panels in the fence after $t$ hours. Then,\n\n$$\n{P}^{′}(t)=\\frac{\\text{d}P(t)}{\\text{d}t}=\\frac{\\text{Change in }P}{\\text{Change in }t}.\n$$\n\nThus, ${P}^{′}(t)$ gives the rate at which the number of panels increases at time $t$, which is the same as $r(t).$ Therefore, the relationship between $P(t)$ and $r(t)$ is ${P}^{′}(t)=r(t).$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186247284 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "022f3b45-6eba-59cd-ac96-d1dfcb9395b5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{N}^{′}(t)=E(t)+L(t)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186244325} {:answer/id #uuid "38f59574-01db-50b0-97d7-bc444b6a4d78" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{N}^{′}(t)=E(t)-L(t)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186244818} {:answer/id #uuid "6aea9487-58e2-53d6-bf2e-05490db0bd2a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "N(t)=E(t)+L(t)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245261} {:answer/id #uuid "72e6a58d-87d0-5d92-aa91-ffbcb278debd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "N(t)=E(t)-L(t)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245340} {:answer/id #uuid "7d934b23-0ed6-589c-ad01-00a583f0a994" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{N}^{′}(t)=E(t)\\cdot L(t)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245416}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "38f59574-01db-50b0-97d7-bc444b6a4d78" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{N}^{′}(t)=E(t)-L(t)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186244818} :answer-field/id #uuid "23d223b5-bd3f-5c3b-89d6-23c60d550968" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186246607}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "e51a9487-572c-5eee-b066-402d8c949221" :question/math-academy-id "q-112519" :question/problem "To measure the number of children visiting a playground, Noah uses the following three functions that model the hourly number of visitors to the playground $t$ hours after the playground is opened to the public.\n\n- $N(t)$ - the number of children inside the playground\n\n- $E(t)$ - the rate at which children enter the playground\n\n- $L(t)$ - the rate at which children leave the playground\n\nWhat is the relationship between the functions above?" :question/worked-solution "The function $N(t)$ gives the number of children inside the park $t$ minutes after opening. Then,\n\n$$\n{N}^{′}(t)=\\frac{\\text{d}N(t)}{\\text{d}t}=\\frac{\\text{Change in }N}{\\text{Change in }t}.\n$$\n\nThus, ${N}^{′}(t)$ gives the rate at which the number of children inside the playground changes $t$ hours after opening.\n\nIn addition, we can compute the rate of change of the number of children inside the playground at time $t$ by finding the difference between the entry and exit rates at time $t.$ That is,\n\n$$\n{N}^{′}(t)=E(t)-L(t).\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186247285 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "51117387-838c-5ae1-a569-486ef5d058e9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "N(t)=-O(t)-C(t)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245033} {:answer/id #uuid "59f937e3-e9b5-5c9e-94e3-63a6aa799141" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "N(t)=O(t)+C(t)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245103} {:answer/id #uuid "911ba7f6-851c-5f58-a5fc-5068dd99b23c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{N}^{′}(t)=O(t)+C(t)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245583} {:answer/id #uuid "ea6976e0-a6e8-5f02-9bbb-665b9dd2e489" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{N}^{′}(t)=O(t)-C(t)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186246393} {:answer/id #uuid "fe3ebe34-c337-5e89-b070-255a338cea0f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "N(t)=O(t)-C(t)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186246537}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ea6976e0-a6e8-5f02-9bbb-665b9dd2e489" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{N}^{′}(t)=O(t)-C(t)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186246393} :answer-field/id #uuid "5637c519-0dcb-5ebf-8eff-71f832658838" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186246698}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "a8187edc-1d98-57d1-8d80-0dd8b47814cc" :question/math-academy-id "q-112522" :question/problem "Oliver, the owner of a platform for chess players, uses the following three functions to model the daily number of users of the platform $t$ days after it was launched.\n\n- $N(t)$ - the number of users with an account\n\n- $O(t)$ - the rate at which new users open an account\n\n- $C(t)$ - the rate at which users cancel their account\n\nWhat is the relationship between the three functions above?" :question/worked-solution "The function $N(t)$ gives the number of users $t$ days after the platform is set up. Then,\n\n$$\n{N}^{′}(t)=\\frac{\\text{d}N(t)}{\\text{d}t}=\\frac{\\text{Change in }N}{\\text{Change in }t}.\n$$\n\nThus, ${N}^{′}(t)$ gives the rate at which the number of users with an account changes $t$ days after opening.\n\nIn addition, we can compute the rate of change of the number of users at time $t$ by finding the difference between the open and cancel rates at time $t.$ That is,\n\n$$\n{N}^{′}(t)=O(t)-C(t).\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186339060 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1bd3314e-09b5-5ed6-b34d-9c8eb2cd078f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{A}^{′}(t)=r(t)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186336291} {:answer/id #uuid "5f89b95a-dc2f-5355-a891-5f7ad0897f2f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "A(t)=-{r}^{′}(t)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186336898} {:answer/id #uuid "d84adbce-e1e5-541f-ae42-248e49f85aef" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{A}^{′}(t)=-r(t)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337909} {:answer/id #uuid "eb90804a-9cb1-5c0e-93ff-93893405ab87" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "A(t)={r}^{′}(t)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338088} {:answer/id #uuid "f843d514-c114-567f-8b4e-d0d7f91897e0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "A(t)=r(t)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338207}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1bd3314e-09b5-5ed6-b34d-9c8eb2cd078f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{A}^{′}(t)=r(t)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186336291} :answer-field/id #uuid "27c52aef-834f-5c1c-9709-b11a313c17d7" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338353}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "4da77317-b047-59f4-8384-7a00ca57d0df" :question/math-academy-id "q-72105" :question/problem "Douglas, a pilot, is flying a plane. The plane's control systems record two measurements for different values of $t,$ where $t$ is the time, in minutes, since take off. The two measurements are:\n\n- $A(t)$ - the altitude (height) of the plane\n\n- $r(t)$ the rate at which the altitude is increasing\n\nWhat is the relationship between $A(t)$ and $r(t)?$" :question/worked-solution "The function $A(t)$ gives the altitude of the plane after $t$ hours. Then,\n\n$$\n{A}^{′}(t)=\\frac{\\text{d}A(t)}{\\text{d}t}=\\frac{\\text{Change in }A}{\\text{Change in }t}.\n$$\n\nThus, ${A}^{′}(t)$ gives the rate at which the altitude is increasing at time $t$, which is the same as $r(t).$ Therefore, the relationship between $A(t)$ and $r(t)$ is ${A}^{′}(t)=r(t).$"}] :knowledge-point/title "Relating a Derivative to a Rate of Change"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064274 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064117 :question/id #uuid "aaeb0407-771b-5dbc-8a50-e7bc0e3477c3" :question/math-academy-id "e-6209" :question/problem "Evaluate $\\displaystyle \\int_0^{\\pi/5} x\\sin(5x) \\, \\textrm{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "Let's use integration by parts. We set\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=x\\, & ⟹\\,{u}^{′}=1 \\\\ {v}^{′}=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5x) & ⟹\\,v=-\\frac{1}{5}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5x).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above into the integration by parts formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x & =uv-\\int v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int x\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡(5x)\\,\\text{d}x & =-x\\cdot \\frac{1}{5}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5x)-\\int (-\\frac{1}{5}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5x))\\cdot 1\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we evaluate the integral and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /5}x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5x)\\,\\text{d}x & =-{\\frac{1}{5}x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5x)|}_{0}^{\\pi /5}+\\frac{1}{5}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /5}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-{\\frac{1}{5}x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5x)|}_{0}^{\\pi /5}+{\\frac{1}{5}(\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5x)}{5})|}_{0}^{\\pi /5} \\\\  & =[-\\frac{1}{5}\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{5}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\pi )+\\frac{1}{5}\\cdot 0\\cdot \\operatorname{cos}⁡(0)]+[\\frac{1}{25}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\pi )-\\frac{1}{25}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(0)] \\\\  & =[-\\frac{\\pi }{25}\\cdot (-1)+0]+[0-0] \\\\  & =\\frac{\\pi }{25}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "d3aaba0a-3b86-58c3-bbc8-22ced09bc8a8" :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064877 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "398c3cee-657c-5b95-8a1e-1aa70b615cd8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\pi -1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330468} {:answer/id #uuid "4b6624a0-3597-520a-b136-40dc699a2c1b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{4}-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330632} {:answer/id #uuid "829fe91a-9a59-5b71-9364-170b07c5eb54" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{2}-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331102} {:answer/id #uuid "b6aee3a4-6d54-578c-8449-e0741c41a98f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\pi -1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331563} {:answer/id #uuid "cea8bab6-1bfc-5d6a-a36b-eda9ee31a503" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi -1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331783}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "829fe91a-9a59-5b71-9364-170b07c5eb54" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{2}-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331102} :answer-field/id #uuid "a32b33d9-9824-5fca-9f78-08bd81319767" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186332487}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "d08b82b1-573b-56aa-9196-6973e5625acf" :question/math-academy-id "q-49664" :question/problem "Evaluate the integral ${\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)\\,\\text{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "Let's use integration by parts. We set\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=x & ⇒ & {u}^{′}=1 \\\\ {v}^{′}=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x) & ⇒ & v=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above into the integration by parts formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x & =uv-\\int v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int x\\cdot \\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)\\,\\text{d}x & =x\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)-\\int \\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)\\cdot 1\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we evaluate the integral and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)\\,\\text{d}x & =x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x){|}_{0}^{\\pi /2}-{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x){|}_{0}^{\\pi /2}+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x){|}_{0}^{\\pi /2} \\\\  & =[\\frac{\\pi }{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2})-0\\operatorname{sin}⁡(0)]+[\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2})-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(0)] \\\\  & =[\\frac{\\pi }{2}-0]+[0-1] \\\\  & =\\frac{\\pi }{2}-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064878 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "50e635c6-8362-502a-8dac-9f4c126f56b3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{9}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330682} {:answer/id #uuid "5b2cbd9a-7afc-5459-b6df-7ca6506a12c9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4}{9}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330765} {:answer/id #uuid "9f4d14d4-eed1-5e2e-b017-564cb00a0993" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{9e}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331378} {:answer/id #uuid "cb8743c8-cccb-54cd-b8ac-95180b80ba0a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2e}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331757} {:answer/id #uuid "cd91e0dd-3fb4-57cb-8cdd-dff11939eaf2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{9}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331772}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "cd91e0dd-3fb4-57cb-8cdd-dff11939eaf2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{9}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331772} :answer-field/id #uuid "4dfe59be-f622-58ca-a168-a466d2025ba6" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186332341}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "49de41a8-b520-5e5d-99f3-b4a02784a3b8" :question/math-academy-id "q-49684" :question/problem "Evaluate the integral ${\\int }_{0}^{1/3}2x{e}^{3x}\\,\\text{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "Let's use integration by parts. We set\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=2x & ⇒ & {u}^{′}=2 \\\\ {v}^{′}={e}^{3x} & ⇒ & v=\\frac{{e}^{3x}}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above into the integration by parts formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x & =uv-\\int v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int 2x\\cdot {e}^{3x}\\,\\text{d}x & =2x\\cdot \\frac{{e}^{3x}}{3}-\\int (\\frac{{e}^{3x}}{3})\\cdot 2\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we evaluate the integral and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1/3}2x{e}^{3x}\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\frac{2}{3}x{e}^{3x}|}_{0}^{1/3}-\\frac{2}{3}{\\int }_{0}^{1/3}{e}^{3x}\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\frac{2}{3}x{e}^{3x}|}_{0}^{1/3}-{\\frac{2}{9}{e}^{3x}|}_{0}^{1/3} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{3}[\\frac{1}{3}{e}^{3(1/3)}-0\\cdot {e}^{3\\cdot 0}]-\\frac{2}{9}[{e}^{3(1/3)}-{e}^{3\\cdot 0}] \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{3}[\\frac{e}{3}-0]-\\frac{2}{9}[e-1] \\\\  & =\\frac{2e}{9}-\\frac{2e}{9}+\\frac{2}{9} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{9}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186250239 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "771a4680-23b4-5532-bdca-e5e5e51c2e8a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{5}{4}({e}^{2}+1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248472} {:answer/id #uuid "788019d8-4726-57ee-8d3c-f8c472f663ea" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{4}({e}^{2}+1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248481} {:answer/id #uuid "938dda6d-62d5-5932-8236-a8efaf7f79ec" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4}({e}^{2}+1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248736} {:answer/id #uuid "aa8bee3f-8a28-593e-a9b3-8c87ee384d6f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{3}{4}({e}^{2}+1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248941} {:answer/id #uuid "ac64494d-e051-58cd-912e-6906743c182e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{4}({e}^{2}+1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248962}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "aa8bee3f-8a28-593e-a9b3-8c87ee384d6f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{3}{4}({e}^{2}+1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248941} :answer-field/id #uuid "7cc9c08d-e5e1-5b3f-9652-c2d450c9f225" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249886}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "ecbdeecb-1f0c-572b-8510-8e18414c1281" :question/math-academy-id "q-114320" :question/problem "Evaluate ${\\int }_{-1}^{0}3x{e}^{-2x}\\,\\text{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "Let's use integration by parts. We set\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=3x & ⇒ & {u}^{′}=3 \\\\ {v}^{′}={e}^{-2x} & ⇒ & v=-\\frac{{e}^{-2x}}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above into the integration by parts formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x & =uv-\\int v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int 3x\\cdot {e}^{-2x}\\,\\text{d}x & =3x\\cdot (-\\frac{{e}^{-2x}}{2})-\\int (-\\frac{{e}^{-2x}}{2})\\cdot 3\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-\\frac{3x{e}^{-2x}}{2}+\\frac{3}{2}\\int {e}^{-2x}\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we evaluate the integral and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-1}^{0}3x{e}^{-2x}\\,\\text{d}x & =-\\frac{3x{e}^{-2x}}{2}{|}_{-1}^{0}+\\frac{3}{2}{\\int }_{-1}^{0}{e}^{-2x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-\\frac{3x{e}^{-2x}}{2}{|}_{-1}^{0}-\\frac{3}{4}{e}^{-2x}{|}_{-1}^{0} \\\\  & =-\\frac{3}{2}[0{e}^{-2(0)}-(-1){e}^{-2(-1)}]-\\frac{3}{4}[{e}^{-2(0)}-{e}^{-2(-1)}] \\\\  & =-\\frac{3}{2}[0+{e}^{2}]-\\frac{3}{4}[1-{e}^{2}] \\\\  & =-\\frac{3}{2}{e}^{2}-\\frac{3}{4}+\\frac{3}{4}{e}^{2} \\\\  & =-\\frac{3}{4}{e}^{2}-\\frac{3}{4} \\\\  & =-\\frac{3}{4}({e}^{2}+1).\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186250240 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4e72326f-b37b-556e-9771-d69f461e0b0f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248129} {:answer/id #uuid "5979c57e-1a61-504f-9748-c153fbd57b43" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{\\pi }{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248234} {:answer/id #uuid "82511b39-0f0e-5f20-82f8-c82314f7aca7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{5\\pi }{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248578} {:answer/id #uuid "941618c9-aa44-56dd-b179-4d773a5937a3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{\\pi }{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248740} {:answer/id #uuid "d4f13165-476e-58f7-beb6-a83b3ddfdb39" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3\\pi }{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249309}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5979c57e-1a61-504f-9748-c153fbd57b43" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{\\pi }{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248234} :answer-field/id #uuid "8956bd65-6e03-5145-875e-cd65f5f6055b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249909}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "b71aa220-d93a-5e59-b207-8dade0373ae4" :question/math-academy-id "q-114322" :question/problem "${\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4x)\\,\\text{d}x=$" :question/worked-solution "Let's use integration by parts. We set\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=x\\, & ⟹\\,{u}^{′}=1 \\\\ {v}^{′}=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4x) & ⟹\\,v=-\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4x).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above into the integration by parts formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x & =uv-\\int v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int x\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡(4x)\\,\\text{d}x & =x\\cdot (-\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4x))-\\int (-\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4x))\\cdot 1\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-\\frac{x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4x)}{4}+\\frac{1}{4}\\int \\operatorname{cos}⁡(4x)\\,\\text{d}x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we evaluate the integral and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4x)\\,\\text{d}x & ={-\\frac{x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4x)}{4}|}_{0}^{\\pi }+\\frac{1}{4}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={-\\frac{x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4x)}{4}|}_{0}^{\\pi }+{\\frac{1}{16}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4x)|}_{0}^{\\pi } \\\\  & =[-\\frac{\\pi \\operatorname{cos}⁡(4\\pi )}{4}+\\frac{0\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4\\cdot 0)}{4}] \\\\  & +\\frac{1}{16}[\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4\\pi )-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4\\cdot 0)] \\\\  & =(-\\frac{\\pi }{4}+0)+\\frac{1}{16}(0-0) \\\\  & =-\\frac{\\pi }{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186250242 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0d83e583-d218-50f4-abb7-474c6d01c304" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{6}+\\frac{1}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247546} {:answer/id #uuid "3d047995-440b-51a6-837d-6a9c0a9dea33" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{\\pi }{3}+\\frac{1}{9}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247961} {:answer/id #uuid "4217347b-9b32-5330-8c51-bcd370f084c2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{\\pi }{6}-\\frac{1}{9}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248013} {:answer/id #uuid "8c7776ae-27e1-5fb2-91d8-1d3d11b460fa" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{\\pi }{6}+\\frac{1}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248680} {:answer/id #uuid "aea67226-a698-5829-a7e0-c9089694e776" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{3}-\\frac{1}{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248983}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4217347b-9b32-5330-8c51-bcd370f084c2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{\\pi }{6}-\\frac{1}{9}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248013} :answer-field/id #uuid "4ff430e6-479c-5fff-ae3c-19a79a5cfe3a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249818}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "37affd24-3b4f-536c-8927-723157249685" :question/math-academy-id "q-114328" :question/problem "${\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)\\,\\text{d}x=$" :question/worked-solution "Let's use integration by parts. We set\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=x & ⇒ & {u}^{′}=1 \\\\ {v}^{′}=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x) & ⇒ & v=\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above into the integration by parts formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x & =uv-\\int v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int x\\cdot \\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)\\,\\text{d}x & =x\\cdot \\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)}{3}-\\int \\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)}{3}\\cdot 1\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we evaluate the integral and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\frac{x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)}{3}|}_{0}^{\\pi /2}-{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)}{3}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\frac{1}{3}x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)|}_{0}^{\\pi /2}+\\frac{1}{9}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x){|}_{0}^{\\pi /2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}[\\frac{\\pi }{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{3\\pi }{2})-0\\operatorname{sin}⁡(0)] \\\\  & +\\frac{1}{9}[\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{3\\pi }{2})-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(0)] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}(-\\frac{\\pi }{2}-0)+\\frac{1}{9}(0-1) \\\\  & =-\\frac{\\pi }{6}-\\frac{1}{9}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186250243 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "77d8920c-9eae-5d0e-8971-ca7e7b55533e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2e-3}{e}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248477} {:answer/id #uuid "7b577e2d-1a9b-598e-a5bb-8e6d22918919" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{e-2}{e+2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248506} {:answer/id #uuid "82f9258b-b72f-566d-a506-e8c7094ed4bd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{e+1}{e}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248582} {:answer/id #uuid "b4d80631-c8d5-5425-9e65-8029a411c1a1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{e-2}{e}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249042} {:answer/id #uuid "fb407c98-f1d8-5183-b7e1-e23543be95c5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{e}{e+2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249609}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b4d80631-c8d5-5425-9e65-8029a411c1a1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{e-2}{e}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249042} :answer-field/id #uuid "cf81a2af-d8b3-5358-9ec2-8ae5505c5bd0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/